#. Tag: title
#: filemng.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "The File Manager"
msgstr "The File Manager"

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde;'s file manager is &konqueror;. The &konqueror; home page is located at "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.konqueror.org\">http://www.konqueror.org</ulink> "
"where a &konqueror; specific <acronym>FAQ</acronym> can be found."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I change the appearance of a folder in &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Right-click the folder, select <guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem>"
", click on the large icon in the dialog which appears, and choose another icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the icon displayed for entries in the <guimenu>K Menu</guimenu>"
", use the <application>Menu Editor</application>, located at <menuchoice>"
"<guisubmenu>Settings</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Menu Editor</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I do non-anonymous &FTP; transfers with &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally, if you enter a &URL; like <userinput>ftp://<replaceable>"
"ftp.somehost.com</replaceable></userinput>, &konqueror; will attempt an "
"anonymous login to the &FTP; server. If you want to login as a particular user, "
"enter a &URL; like "
"<userinput>ftp://<replaceable>username@ftp.somehost.com</replaceable>"
"</userinput> instead. &konqueror; will ask for your password and connect to the "
"server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I specify the startup folder for &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the &RMB;, click on the Home icon and choose <guimenuitem>"
"Properties</guimenuitem>. Under the <guilabel>Application</guilabel> "
"tab you will probably find something like <command>kfmclient openProfile "
"filemanagement</command>; just append <filename class=\"directory\">"
"file:/whereever/you/want</filename> with the folder you would like &konqueror; "
"to start in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I rename files?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> click on the file and select "
"<guimenuitem>Rename</guimenuitem> or press the keyboard shortcut <keycap>"
"F2</keycap> with a file selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where did the delete entry from my right-click context menu go?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kde; 3.4 the delete context menu entries that bypass the trashcan are no "
"longer displayed by default. To enable them, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &konqueror;</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"and select <guilabel>Behaviour</guilabel> in the iconbar to the left. Tick the "
"checkbox <guilabel>Show 'Delete' context menu entries which bypass the "
"trashcan</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I configure the programs that &konqueror; uses to open different types "
"of files?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to configure file associations, you should go to the &kcontrolcenter; "
"and choose the item <guimenuitem>File Associations</guimenuitem> "
"under the category <guimenu>KDE Components</guimenu>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Suppose the default <acronym>PDF</acronym> viewer is now &kghostview; and you "
"would prefer to use <application>KPDF</application> as a viewer. You would "
"simply type <userinput>pdf</userinput> in the search box at the top of the "
"dialog, choose <guimenuitem>pdf</guimenuitem> in the <guimenu>"
"application</guimenu> group and move <application>KPDF</application> "
"up. In the <guilabel>Embedding</guilabel> tab you can also choose which "
"component other applications will use to display files (for example, when "
"viewing files in &konqueror; or using &ark;'s embedded viewer)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I try to click on a folder in &konqueror;, I get the message: <quote>"
"There appears to be a configuration error. You have associated Konqueror with "
"inode/directory, but it cannot handle this file type.</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You need to make sure that the embedding settings for inode/directory are "
"correct:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &konqueror;, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Configure Konqueror</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and then to the <guilabel>"
"File Associations</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open inode->directory in the tree view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guilabel>Embedding</guilabel> tab. Make sure that <guilabel>"
"Left Click Action</guilabel> is set to <guilabel>Show file in embedded "
"viewer</guilabel>, and by default <guilabel>Icon View (konq_iconview)</guilabel> "
"is at the top of <guilabel>Services Preference Order.</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What are <option>%i</option> and <option>%m</option> in the Execute line?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"They are used by all &kde; applications (since they are implemented in "
"<classname>KApplication</classname> and all good &kde; programs create a "
"<classname>KApplication</classname> object before they even look at the command "
"line arguments)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A standard line for a &kde; application looks like this: <userinput><command>"
"foo</command> <option>... %i %m -caption \\\"%c\\\"</option></userinput>"
". Pretty confusing, -but it has been designed in that way so that it can "
"integrate legacy, non-&kde; applications as smoothly as possible. &konqueror;, "
"when executing the line above, will extend the command to <userinput><command>"
"<replaceable>foo</replaceable></command> <option>-icon something.png -miniicon "
"something_mini.png -caption \\\"The Foo\\\"</option></userinput>"
". Both the icon and the mini-icon as well as \"The Foo\" are properties defined "
"in the <filename>.desktop</filename> file. If the icons are not defined, they "
"simply default to the executable name <replaceable>foo</replaceable>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This way a user can change these things in &kmenuedit; for his or her "
"applications. The <option>-caption</option> option is important, because no "
"user will accept that the menu item <guimenuitem>Editor</guimenuitem> "
"starts something called <guilabel>kedit-0.9pl4-build47</guilabel>"
". Instead, he expects a window called <guilabel>Editor</guilabel>"
". Furthermore these names are localized, <abbrev>i.e.</abbrev> "
"an American user launches <guimenuitem>CD-Player</guimenuitem> "
"and gets a window called <guilabel>CD-Player</guilabel> "
"while a German user launches <guimenuitem>CD-Spieler</guimenuitem> "
"and gets a window called <guilabel>CD-Spieler</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I make &konqueror; start up without a menu bar? I can't save a view "
"profile when the menu bar is invisible!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to do this is to edit &konqueror;'s configuration file "
"manually. Add the following lines to "
"<filename>~/.kde/share/config/konquerorrc</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: filemng.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KonqMainWindow]\n"
"MenuBar=Disabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "On restarting &konqueror;, the menubar should be hidden."
msgstr ""
